From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:53:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] bcm53xx: nvram: add Netgear R8000 BCM43602 board-ID and
 LED entries

The bcm53xx nvram-init table already special-cases the near-identical
ASUS RT-AC3200 (same BCM43602 chip family, same triple-radio board
layout) but had no entry at all for the Netgear R8000, so brcmfmac was
never bound with per-radio devid/sromrev/boardrev/boardflags/devpath
values and the 5 GHz radios (and in practice the whole Wi-Fi subsystem)
never came up correctly.

Adds a netgear,r8000 case to both set_bcm43602_variables() (the
per-radio board-ID binding for all three BCM43602 radios) and
set_wireless_led_behaviour() (the matching LED mode). The board-ID
values are per-model constants (chip wiring, not per-unit calibration)
extracted from a physical R8000 unit by the 88plug/netgear-r8000-plus
project; actual per-unit calibration and MAC addresses keep coming from
the preserved factory 0:ART partition, untouched by this patch.

Upstream had concluded (openwrt/openwrt#20514) this was unrecoverable,
proprietary 5 GHz calibration baked into the driver binary. It is not:
it is simply a missing board-ID table entry, the same class of fix the
table already carries for several other boards.

No controlled A/B test (flash stock, compare) was run to prove this is
the sole cause of 5 GHz working - treat as a well-targeted, low-risk fix
based on one unit's extracted values, not an independently confirmed root
cause for every unit/revision.
---
 package/utils/nvram/files/nvram-bcm53xx.init | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/utils/nvram/files/nvram-bcm53xx.init b/package/utils/nvram/files/nvram-bcm53xx.init
index d87574f..e20fcd8 100644
--- a/package/utils/nvram/files/nvram-bcm53xx.init
+++ b/package/utils/nvram/files/nvram-bcm53xx.init
@@ -36,6 +36,10 @@ set_wireless_led_behaviour() {
 			COMMIT=1
 			nvram set 0:ledbh10=0x7 set 1:ledbh10=0x7
 			;;
+		netgear,r8000)
+			COMMIT=1
+			nvram set 0:ledbh10=0x7 set 1:ledbh10=0x7 set 2:ledbh10=0x7
+			;;
 	esac
 }
 
@@ -68,6 +72,36 @@ set_bcm43602_variables() {
 			nvram set 2:sromrev=11
 			nvram set 2:boardflags=0x30040000
 			;;
+		netgear,r8000)
+			COMMIT=1
+
+			# radio 0 (5 GHz) - BCM43602
+			nvram set devpath0=pcie/1/1
+			nvram set 0:devpath0=sb/1/
+			nvram set 0:devid=0x43bc
+			nvram set 0:boardrev=0x1421
+			nvram set 0:sromrev=11
+			nvram set 0:boardflags=0x30008000
+			nvram set 0:boardflags2=0x2
+
+			# radio 1 (2.4 GHz) - BCM43602
+			nvram set devpath1=pcie/2/3
+			nvram set 1:devpath1=sb/1/
+			nvram set 1:devid=0x43bb
+			nvram set 1:boardrev=0x1421
+			nvram set 1:sromrev=11
+			nvram set 1:boardflags=0x1000
+			nvram set 1:boardflags2=0x2
+
+			# radio 2 (5 GHz) - BCM43602
+			nvram set devpath2=pcie/2/4
+			nvram set 2:devpath2=sb/1/
+			nvram set 2:devid=0x43bc
+			nvram set 2:boardrev=0x1421
+			nvram set 2:sromrev=11
+			nvram set 2:boardflags=0x10000000
+			nvram set 2:boardflags2=0x2
+			;;
 	esac
 }
 
